# Strike an acid blob from TWO squares away with a glaive, and read the
# glaive's own description page before and after (bd inc-m2zi, seed-proofed by inc-drr0).
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22-maxhp.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/orc-warrior-dequ-seed5-maxhp.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/dequ-reach.keys 5
#
# WHAT IS BEING MEASURED. Before this change the loop in Creature::Strike that
# looks for response attacks was skipped entirely unless the victim was BESIDE
# the striker, so a glaive user striking from two squares away took no A_DEQU
# retaliation at all. The retaliation now fires at whatever distance the blow
# was struck from.
#
# THE ABSENCE OF A MESSAGE IS WHAT THE OLD BEHAVIOUR LOOKED LIKE, so this run
# has to prove the positive. Three things are dumped: the map, on which the
# character and the blob are two squares apart with open floor between them;
# the strike screen, which must name the blob and say the blow landed; and the
# glaive's page before and after, which must lose hit points.
#
# WHY A GLAIVE. It is an iron polearm carrying WT_REACH (lib/weapons.irh:192),
# so wielding it sets MS_HAS_REACH, and a direction key then attacks a creature
# two squares away instead of walking (src/Player.cpp:1335-1339).
#
# ONE BLOB, THREE BLOWS. The check forces the character's damage to its minimum
# (INCURSION_FORCE_DAMAGE_ROLL=1: every blow and every acid splash is minimum) and doubles
# the blob's hit points (OPT_MON_MAX_HP in the options file), so the blob
# survives all three blows and answers each one. The blob is summoned two
# squares east, which is also where the blows are aimed, so the character never
# moves.
#
# THE CHARACTER IS LOADED (INCURSION_LOAD, set by tools/check_dequ_reach.sh):
# tools/fixtures/chars/orc-warrior-dequ-seed5-maxhp.sav. This script does what
# dequ-setup.keys does after chargen: wizard mode on, the level cleared with
# Genocide Everything, Freeze Monsters on. Freeze Monsters keeps the blob still;
# it still ANSWERS a blow, because A_DEQU fires from inside the resolution of
# the player's own attack.

@until "Things in View" ESC

# 'w' opens wizard mode and 'y' confirms it the first time.
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w y
@choose "Genocide Everything"
SPACE*40                 # dismiss the genocide message chain; the level is then empty

@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
# The switch list draws no cursor a screen dump can see, so this counts rows:
# Freeze Monsters is the eleventh, and the cursor opens on the first.
@expect "Freeze Monsters"
DOWN*10
@expect "all monsters are denied their"
SPACE                    # Freeze Monsters: NO -> YES
@expect "Wizard Mode Options"
ESC                      # Close the switches list.
@until "Things in View" ESC

# The starting kit now readies a shield, and a two-handed weapon will not go
# into a hand pair that holds one (inc-zzwm): stow it before the swap below.
@until "SPACE:Swap" i
@until ">>a)Ready" a
s
@until "Things in View" ESC

w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*9                 # walk the glyph row to ordinary weapons
@until "Glaive" DOWN
DOWN                    # the wanted row is the middle of three; step onto it
ENTER
b                       # Weapon Hand -- the slot lettering skips 'd' (Drop)
SPACE                   # swap the glaive into it
@while "two-handed" y
s                       # stow the starting knife the swap pushed into the air
@until "SPACE:Swap" i    # the inventory manager, if it is not already open
@until ">>b)Weapon" b    # select the Weapon Hand
@until "base value of" x # Examine: the item's own description page
@dump:reach-before
@until "Things in View" ESC

# Two squares east, not one: RIGHT RIGHT walks the summoning cursor out to the
# square the reach attack will reach.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Jellies"
@choose "acid blob"
RIGHT RIGHT ENTER
@dump:reach-placed
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@dump:reach-strike-1

RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@dump:reach-strike-2

RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@dump:reach-strike-3

@until "SPACE:Swap" i
@until ">>b)Weapon" b
@until "base value of" x
@dump:reach-after
@until "Things in View" ESC
@quit
